# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Visit alert (demo open-tracking) — Web3Forms access key
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The deployed demo sends a one-time "someone opened the site" email via
# Web3Forms (https://web3forms.com). Web3Forms delivers each submission to the
# email address that OWNS the access key — there is no recipient field in the
# code. So the alerts only reach the right inbox if this key was created at
# https://web3forms.com using the address  francis@creativedevlabs.com .
#
# Create a free key there with that address, paste it below (and set the same
# variable in your host's environment settings), then rebuild. This value is
# public by design: NEXT_PUBLIC_ vars are inlined into the browser bundle, so
# it is NOT a secret and whoever created the key controls where mail goes.
#
# Leave it empty to disable visit alerts entirely (the site works normally).
NEXT_PUBLIC_WEB3FORMS_KEY=
